    "body": "Notation-only changes to the overview section. They are:\r\n\r\nP<sub>i</sub> -> P<sub>k</sub>. The index i is never defined, and the output is derived from the counter k.\r\n\r\nDefine A = a·G right after a is redefined as the sum of the input private keys. Then use A in input_hash = hash(outpoint<sub>L</sub> || A) instead of (a·G). The BIP uses uppercase for public keys, and this was the only place where a public key appeared in the middle of an operation as (a·G). It also matches the sender spec, which writes \"A = a·G\".",
    "labels": [
      {
